check-*.py
# Whitelist the crisis-hotline pre-push guard (MAINT-154) — it's a permanent
# safety check, not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!app/scripts/check-crisis-hotline.js
!app/__tests__/scripts/check-crisis-hotline.test.js

# Same carve-out, DEBUG-389. NOTE FOR WHOEVER ADDS THE NEXT ONE: the blanket
# `check-*.js` above was written for ad-hoc developer scratch scripts, but it
# catches every permanent guard in app/scripts/ too — and it does so SILENTLY.
# `git add -A` reports nothing, `git status` shows nothing, and the miss only
# surfaces when CI runs the step and the file it names is not in the repo.
# Every permanent guard therefore needs an explicit un-ignore here. The ones
# already tracked (check-breathing-worklet-purity, check-ci-test-coverage,
# check-crisis-dial-guard) are tracked only because someone force-added them,
# so this list reads shorter than the real set.
!app/scripts/check-workflow-scripts.js
!app/__tests__/scripts/check-workflow-scripts.test.js
# Whitelist the service-singleton setInterval guard check (INFRA-177) —
# CI-enforced convention guard, not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!scripts/check-service-interval-guards.js
# Whitelist the CI test-coverage ledger (INFRA-368) — CI-enforced gate, not an
# ad-hoc developer scratch script. Without these two lines the `check-*.js` rule
# above silently swallows both files, and the CI step added by INFRA-368 would
# invoke a script that is not in the repository.
#
# Every permanent guard script in this repo has an entry in this negation block;
# there is no force-added exception. Adding one is the convention, not a
# workaround — the failure it prevents is silent, since `git add .` simply does
# not stage an ignored file and reports nothing.
!app/scripts/check-ci-test-coverage.js
# Whitelist the crisis keyboard-accessory guard (DEBUG-450) — a CI-enforced safety
# gate (Security + compliance), not an ad-hoc developer scratch script. A jest suite
# imports it too, so without this line BOTH that step and `Crisis authority
# validation` fail with MODULE_NOT_FOUND while every local check passes.
!app/scripts/check-crisis-keyboard-accessory-guard.js
!app/__tests__/scripts/check-ci-test-coverage.test.js
# Whitelist the breathing-worklet purity guard (INFRA-306) — CI-enforced
# structural guard on the animation path, not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!app/scripts/check-breathing-worklet-purity.js
# Whitelist the crisis-dial guard (DEBUG-314) — pins every tel:/sms: dial to
# openCrisisUrl. Enforced both in precommit (via __tests__/safety) and in the
# CI security job, not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!app/scripts/check-crisis-dial-guard.js
# Whitelist the modal-occlusion guard (DEBUG-406) — fails on any RN <Modal> in
# app/src outside a recorded allowlist, because a <Modal> renders in a separate
# native window above the root crisis button and produces a zero-988-affordance
# state. Enforced in precommit (via __tests__/safety) and in the CI security
# job, not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!app/scripts/check-modal-occlusion-guard.js
!app/__tests__/scripts/check-breathing-worklet-purity.test.js
# Whitelist the SafeAreaView core-import guard (MAINT-437) — CI-enforced via
# test:scripts. RN's SafeAreaView is iOS-only and applies zero insets on Android,
# where SDK 56 makes edge-to-edge mandatory, so a regression is a silent layout
# defect rather than a warning. Not an ad-hoc developer scratch script.
!app/scripts/check-safe-area-imports.js
!app/__tests__/scripts/check-safe-area-imports.test.js
execute-*.js
